Eco Care Group Pty Ltd
Unit 2/28 Artisan Rd, Seven Hills NSW 2147
Full Time Office Manager 
$78,000 - $85,000 (Commensurate with experience)

SUMMARY
Eco Care Group Pty Ltd is an innovative Australian company formulating, manufacturing and trading first-class cleaning chemicals and other products. Our innovative vision has driven us to forgo standard formulations, striving to develop products that utilise the most cutting-edge technology and biodegradable ingredients. As we continue to expand, we are seeking a competent and experienced Office Manager to take care of our office based in Seven Hills, NSW.
Reporting to management, the Office Manager will be responsible for the day-to-day coordination of our Seven Hills office, ensuring our administrative systems, staff and resources run smoothly in support of Eco Care Group's manufacturing, formulation and trading operations. This is a hands-on, all-rounder role suited to someone who is highly organised, tech-savvy, and comfortable managing a broad range of office and operational responsibilities.

Key Responsibilities 
•	Contributing to the planning and review of office services, and setting priorities and office service standards across the business; 
•	Allocating human resources, office space and equipment to support day-to-day operations; 
•	Assigning work to, and monitoring the performance of, office and administrative staff; 
•	Managing office records and accounts, including documentation related to our product lines, suppliers and customers; 
•	Liaising with professionals such as accountants, suppliers, logistics partners and regulatory bodies to coordinate office business and resolve operational issues; 
•	Ensuring office equipment, IT systems and supplies are properly maintained; 
•	Ensuring compliance with occupational health and safety regulations, including those relevant to a chemical manufacturing and trading environment; 
•	Ensuring office operations comply with relevant government legislation, policies and procedures; and 
•	Coordinating personnel activities such as hiring, promotions, performance management, payroll, training and supervision. 





Required Skills
•	At least 2 years' experience working in a similar office management role; 
•	A competent, hardworking approach and a genuine willingness to learn; 
•	Excellent written and verbal communication skills; 
•	Strong knowledge of online business systems and software; and 
•	A background in IT, accounting/economics, sales, marketing, or supply chain management (highly desirable). 

How to apply:

Applications open on 23 July 2026 and close on 22 August 2026
Please send your CV to info@businessnest.com.au. Please include the job role title in your email.
